course: dictionary
lesson: 7971
title: Words for seats
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A recliner is a soft armchair. Its back can lean back and its footrest can come up, so you can lie back and feel comfortable. The sentence «lean back in the recliner» gives you this clue: you lean back in it.
explain: The word recliner comes from recline, which means to lean back. Recline, reclining and recliner are one word family. When you know one word in a family, you can often work out the others.
explain: The word can also name seats in cars, planes or cinemas that lean back. Look at what the seat does and where it is. That tells you what kind of seat it is.
explain: Read this safety sentence: «Keep fingers clear of the folding parts of recliners and folding chairs, because they pinch and crush.» The words pinch and crush are the clues. Moving parts can hurt your fingers, so keep them clear.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A recliner is a soft armchair whose back leans back and whose footrest comes up.
fact: Recliners can also be car, plane or cinema seats that lean back.
fact: «Recline» means to lean back, and a «reclining seat» is one that leans back.
fact: Recline, reclining and recliner belong to one word family because they share the same root.
exercise: «Grandad sat back in his recliner with a book.» What is a recliner? | A table for eating dinner | A small, hard stool for the kitchen | *A soft armchair whose back can lean back
exercise: «Keep fingers clear of the folding parts of recliners and folding chairs, because they pinch and crush.» Why should you keep fingers clear? | The folding parts are very shiny | They might get cold | *They could get pinched or crushed
exercise: Which word is in the same word family as recline? | cosy | chair | footrest | *reclining
test: «She lay back in the recliner and fell asleep.» What does recliner mean here? | A cupboard for books | A kind of bicycle | *A soft armchair that leans back | A bed for the night
test: Which of these can be a recliner? | *A cinema seat that leans back | A rubbish bin | A kitchen table
exam: What does «reclining seat» most likely mean? | *A seat whose back can lean back | A seat that folds flat into the floor | A seat that is always moving | A wooden seat with no back
